{# The Speed view: the same search against a plain ILIKE, then the benchmark of nine queries on demand. #}
<div class="stack">
    {% if speed %}
        <div class="speed-bars" data-controller="ilike" data-src="{{ path('search_ilike', {q: q, fz: speed.warm|round(3)}) }}">
            <div data-ilike-target="region" aria-busy="true">
                <div class="speed-row">
                    <span>Fuzzphony</span>
                    <span class="speed-bar"><span class="is-fuzzphony" style="width: 2%"></span></span>
                    <span class="speed-value">{{ speed.warm|number_format(1) }} ms</span>
                </div>
                <div class="speed-row">
                    <span>ILIKE</span>
                    <span class="speed-bar"><span class="skeleton" style="width: 100%; height: 100%"></span></span>
                    <span class="speed-value muted">scanning {{ rowEstimate > 0 ? rowEstimate|number_format : 'the catalogue' }} rows…</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <p class="muted">Warm median of {{ warmRuns }} runs after one cold run ({{ speed.cold|number_format(1) }} ms), for the search without its facets. ILIKE is measured the same way, in a request of its own so Fuzzphony's answer never waits for it. <code>ILIKE '%…%'</code> does not rank, fold accents, stem or tolerate typos.</p>
    {% else %}
        <div class="empty"><strong>Nothing to compare yet</strong>Search something, then see how long it takes next to a plain <code>ILIKE</code>.</div>
    {% endif %}

    <section aria-labelledby="bench">
        <h2 id="bench" class="facet-title" style="margin-left: 0">The benchmark</h2>
        {% if not run %}
            <div class="list">
                <div class="row no-lead">
                    <div class="row-body">
                        <div class="row-title">Nine queries, one after the other</div>
                        <div class="row-sub">{{ queries|length }} queries × (1 cold + {{ warmRuns }} warm runs) × {{ engines }} engines = {{ (queries|length * (1 + warmRuns) * engines)|number_format }} statements on {{ rowEstimate > 0 ? rowEstimate|number_format ~ ' products' : 'the catalogue' }}.</div>
                    </div>
                    <a class="button primary" href="{{ path('search', {q: q ?: null, view: 'speed', run: 1}) }}" data-loading-message="Starting the benchmark…">Run it</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        {% else %}
            <p class="muted">20 results per query. Cold is the first run; warm is the median of the next {{ warmRuns }}. <code>ILIKE</code> does not rank and cannot exclude words, so a fast ILIKE row with hits is not the same work.</p>
            {# Every row is measured by its own request, one after the other (sequence controller): the page is usable at once,
               progress is real, and the queries never run in parallel, which would distort the timings. #}
            <div data-controller="sequence" aria-busy="true">
                <div class="run-status">
                    <progress data-sequence-target="progress" value="0" max="{{ queries|length }}" aria-label="Benchmark progress"></progress>
                    <span data-sequence-target="label" role="status">Starting…</span>
                    <a class="button" href="{{ path('search', {q: q ?: null, view: 'speed', run: 1}) }}" data-sequence-target="done" hidden>Run again</a>
                </div>
                <table>
                    <thead><tr><th>Query</th><th class="num">ILIKE cold</th><th class="num">ILIKE warm</th><th class="num">hits</th><th class="num">Fuzzphony cold</th><th class="num">Fuzzphony warm</th><th class="num">hits</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody>
                    {% for label, example in queries %}
                        <tr class="pending-row" data-src="{{ path('benchmark_row', {index: loop.index0}) }}" data-label="{{ label }}">
                            <td>{{ label }}<br><code class="muted">{{ example }}</code></td>
                            {% for i in 1..6 %}<td class="num"><span class="skeleton"></span></td>{% endfor %}
                        </tr>
                    {% endfor %}
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <p class="muted">~ means typo tolerant. Rows are timed one at a time: other requests at the same moment can skew them. Outside the browser: <code>php benchmarks/run.php --markdown</code>.</p>
        {% endif %}
    </section>
</div>
